@startuml priming_timing
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam ArrowFontColor #e6edf7
title Where the 16 ms come from: priming and playback after Start (axis in ms; project calculation, not measured)
concise "i2s0 DMA: microphone fills" as receive
concise "audio thread: processes" as thread
concise "i2s1 DMA: DAC plays" as transmit
scale 4 as 110 pixels
@0
receive is "R1"
thread is {-}
transmit is "silence 1"
@4
receive is "R2"
thread is "R1 to T1"
transmit is "silence 2"
@7
thread is {-}
@8
receive is "R3"
thread is "R2 to T2"
transmit is "silence 3"
@11
thread is {-}
@12
receive is "R4"
thread is "R3 to T3"
transmit is "silence 4"
@15
thread is {-}
@16
receive is "R5"
thread is "R4 to T4"
transmit is "T1"
@19
thread is {-}
@20
receive is "R6"
transmit is "T2"
@24
receive is {-}
transmit is {-}
highlight 7 to 16 #3a3320 : T1 waits in the TX queue
transmit@0 <-> @16 : 16 ms: the sound captured in R1 plays as T1
thread@4 <-> @7 : at most 3 ms (P02)
legend bottom
  Start primes 4 silent TX blocks, then starts RX, then TX (both at t = 0 here; the gap between the two triggers is not measured).
  The thread may start T1 up to 9 ms late and still queue it before 16 ms: 12 ms reserve minus the 3 ms budget.
  Transport delay = 4 primed blocks × 4 ms = 16 ms, constant. Converter filters add 1.08 ms (INMP441) + 1.25 ms (PCM5102A): about 18 ms.
endlegend
@enduml
